{"title":"2024 USAMO Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Day_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Day_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Day 2</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_1\">Day 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Day 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Find all integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that the following property holds: if we list the divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/2149f09cba97fa3185a9a26d4b3185a81a0b376a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n !$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in increasing order as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce12d0865dfd5505a50984e13f541da656e9623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1=d_1&lt;d_2&lt;\\cdots&lt;d_k=n!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"221\" height=\"17\" />, then we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/9/08907a515df771544aa4ddc061d79e8c12f87747.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d_2-d_1 \\leq d_3-d_2 \\leq \\cdots \\leq d_k-d_{k-1}.\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6804dafc1cf3f0701510be7b725aa3ccde83e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" /> be finite sets of integers whose intersection is not empty. For each non-empty <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c3831aa402ffafff3dfaca17ba4b5e02bcab4b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T \\subseteq\\left\\{S_1, S_2, \\ldots, S_{100}\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />, the size of the intersection of the sets in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is a multiple of the number of sets in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. What is the least possible number of elements that are in at least 50 sets?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer. A triangulation of a polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />-balanced if its triangles can be colored with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> colors in such a way that the sum of the areas of all triangles of the same color is the same for each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> colors. Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which there exists an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />-balanced triangulation of a regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon.\n</p><p>Note: A triangulation of a convex polygon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e6a2d706867d6652d7edadccc3fd034130bd98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> sides is any partitioning of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/9/ef9b02e32cfba0db0f9038a8d077596720f62e91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> triangles by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> diagonals of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74f4008768812f46db4b252c9e69cf98c5faaa4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathcal{P}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that do not intersect in the polygon's interior.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Day_2\">Day 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Day 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be positive integers. A circular necklace contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d86988c341f8ccbadc7d344b38e2fedef4a3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"10\" /> beads, each either red or blue. It turned out that no matter how the necklace was cut into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> blocks of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> consecutive beads, each block had a distinct number of red beads. Determine, with proof, all possible values of the ordered pair <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b7e4c455672c30d743cce7506408a40cb68129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is selected inside acute triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b3e28c982dab6e46ca02d25849c3410d5fa170.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A B C$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/c/06c34717463db26d2a54f0adbd1f0061b423a67c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle D A C=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/2/0c276c37b9433ebf2d7a5efc983713e1438f1941.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle A C B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/a/92ab6cdc1e5159821e21bba8f8aa1d7d20384366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle B D C=90^{\\circ}+\\angle B A C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"16\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is chosen on ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/d/79d9297b54cd3ced0a3dbf3f0e395830e944e01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/b/32bf6a5924c5cc24507cdc724b27e32e7b270c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A E=E C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/4/0f48654d3431fa456308c0d1635928f1b086132a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\nShow that line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b5092814adc11bcdc98e23eda01aac125cb98e35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195f9db8181b480a85b388bad0224a8b76a179c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B E M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b9b7a46559a729577c3ca04dd2d7e66de16b3f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> be an integer and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/e/18eecdd2d8a05a3cc1435bc57ff52fcbee7b6e1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell \\in\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />. A collection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd59ab493cf4f21d3f8e1c44db1ff4625eca9d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, \\ldots, A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> of (not necessarily distinct) subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc169aff5a3045cd7bca6cf7050eb325ec1fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" /> is called <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />-large if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/f/c1fc566dbfcd599afd1f71394f3a32318ca4fa34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|A_i\\right| \\geq \\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28c82ec9d7adbeb949d4233e8eadafd3b7d2ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\leq i \\leq k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. Find, in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />, the largest real number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> such that the inequality\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/d/3ed5047ee81526de349e5b0029f19c0187c25429.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^k \\sum_{j=1}^k x_i x_j \\frac{\\left|A_i \\cap A_j\\right|^2}{\\left|A_i\\right| \\cdot\\left|A_j\\right|} \\geq c\\left(\\sum_{i=1}^k x_i\\right)^2\\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"59\" />\nholds for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, all nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/4/124f55009149f42b54d9df5dadddb187f5d7b420.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1, \\ldots, x_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"13\" />, and all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/c/63c17c295325f731666c7d74952b563a01e00fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"9\" height=\"14\" />-large collections <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd59ab493cf4f21d3f8e1c44db1ff4625eca9d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_1, \\ldots, A_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"85\" height=\"18\" /> of subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc169aff5a3045cd7bca6cf7050eb325ec1fb5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2, \\ldots, n\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"98\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note: For a finite set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/3/703d476da77d88fa4cb8a6b30ca4dfcc1a8da95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S,|S|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the number of elements in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO\" title=\"2024 USAMO\">2024 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2024\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems\">2023 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2025 USAMO Problems\">2025 USAMO Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php